Safety section	Check the description against the implicated contracts	**Current candidate: `569ba13c3`.** [Review 5367523337](https://github.com/JKamsker/LiteDB/pull/133#pullrequestreview-5367523337) is fixed: Shared handle callbacks now reject self-dependent native writer acquisition and same-namespace handle admission before waiting. Ordinary work stays unbound; coordinated reads, independent databases, idle-handle handoff and cancellation retain their behavior. All 30 new cases and 46 related guards pass on net8/net10. The strict production proof reproduces six cases on actual `12a057424` and verifies the correction, with eight controls, peer-process writes and cold indexed/sentinel checks on both variants. Independent review also found the adjacent begin case and verified its correction. **Exact-head hosted CI remains in progress.** Fresh production measurements and their independent arithmetic audit are complete below. Earlier green12a results below are historical evidence, not validation of this new head.
Safety section	Check the description against the implicated contracts	
Safety section	Check the description against the implicated contracts	The preceding `f95` run's ARM64 native-crash sharing violation and x64 pinned-writer timeout remain unexplained. Improved capture/progress oracles preserve those original failures and the missing ARM fixture limitation; later green runs do not explain their causes.
