Safety section	Check the description against the implicated contracts	**Only the Shared holder + child-wrapper option is now integrated, with fresh measurements above. All other experiments remain separate and are not included. The numbers in this historical options section describe the original proof branches.** [Full report](https://github.com/JKamsker/LiteDB/blob/t3code/benchmark-group-commit-experiments/docs/transaction-performance-options.md), [controller source and replay instructions](https://github.com/JKamsker/LiteDB/tree/t3code/benchmark-group-commit-experiments/tools/WriteControllerExperiments), and [raw results, traces, exact measured binaries and test evidence](https://github.com/litedb-org/LiteDB-Artifacts/tree/2d58276b767d82d01d894b3af6bceb5048f47bd1/pull-requests/JKamsker-LiteDB-133/2026-09-30-options). All comparisons use production Release/net10.0 with `TestingEnabled=false`, tiering disabled, the same Ubuntu/ext4 host, and alternating fresh-process order. Host load is uncontrolled; these are local descriptive results. No measured samples were discarded.
